  <article xml:id="shorttitlelowercase">
    <title>Math 232 Lecture Notes</title>
<p>Finding the formula for area between curves:</p>
\vspace{5cm}

<p>Example 1. Find the area between the lines <m>f(x) = .5x+5</m> and <m>g(x)=x+.5</m> over the interval <m> [1,5]</m>.</p>
\vvs{3}

<p>Example 2. Find the area bounded between the curves <m>f(x) = 9-(x/2)^2</m> and <m>g(x) = 6-x</m>. </p>
\vvs{3}

<p>Example 3. Find the area between the graphs of <m>f(x) = \sin x</m> and <m>g(x) = \cos x</m> on the interval <m>[0,\pi]</m>.</p>
\vvs{4}

<p>Example 4. Find the area of the region bounded by the curves <m>f(x) = x^2</m> and <m>g(x) = 2 - x</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis.</p>
\vvs{4}

<p>Regions defined with respect to <m>y</m>:</p>
\vvs{3}

<p>Example 5. Find the area of the region bounded by the curves <m>f(x) = x^2</m> and <m>g(x) = 2 - x</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis.</p>
\vvs{5}

<p>Example 6. Find the area of the region bounded by the curves <m>f(x) = \sqrt{x}</m> and <m>g(x) = \frac{3-x}{2}</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis.</p>

  </article>

